  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5951",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the targeting of P2X purinoceptor 7 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin directly interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is a target of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that also targets P2X purinoceptor 7. Similarly, doxorubicin is linked to NCI-H46, which is a target of the same compound, further reinforcing the pathway to P2X purinoceptor 7. This indicates that the interaction between doxorubicin and P2X purinoceptor 7 is mediated through a common intermediate, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. The evidence supports a mechanism where doxorubicin acts through a shared target, suggesting a potential role in modulating P2X purinoceptor activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on this compound, underscoring the complex relationship between doxorubicin and P2X purinoceptor 7.",
